eploy history has only two releases: v5.0.0 (healthy in production) and v5.1.0 (degraded). I rolled payments-api back to **v5.0.0** in all three regions. A follow-up check shows it healthy, with the error rate down to **0.2%**.\n3. **Incident:** My first attempt to open the incident timed out. The incident list was still empty afterwards, so I retried using the same duplicate-protection key, which ensures the request runs at most once. The retry worked: **INC-0001** (SEV2, payments-api) is open and has paged on-call. The summary covers the bad deploy, the rollback and the next steps: confirming recovery and finding what's wrong in v5.1.0.\n\nIf you meant a different payments service, tell me which one. Otherwise, v5.1.0 shouldn't be redeployed until the cause is found and fixed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01PFeD3kJqDMrRBcQoijpu9q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01YHMWphguP5sNWJWyonutNj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VfeBe6Dfoez91shFK6cPHV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_012vr22ALRzHcpG9j9ndPbxB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.5}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01YC2ZoxDBpnr2o6FSBhFxJN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payment-service", "confidence": 0.5}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01S