": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Pn3KegttHARwTDoZasHn85", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-api elevated errors after v5.1.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-api", "summary": "This morning's deploy of payments-api v5.1.0 left the service unhealthy, with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It has been rolled back in all production regions to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. Recovery still needs to be confirmed and the cause in v5.1.0 investigated.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.88}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments back to its last healthy release and opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001.\n\n1. **Finding the service:** There's no service called \"payments\" in the system. The one that matched is **payments-api**. It was running **v5.1.0** in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), was unhealthy, and had an **18% error rate**.\n2. **Rollback:** The deploy history has only two releases: v5.0.0 (healthy in production) and v5.1.0 (degraded). I rolled payments-api back to **v5.0.0** in all three regions. A follow-up check shows it healthy, with the error rate down to **0.2%**.\n3. **Incident:** My first attempt to open the incident timed out. The incident list was still empty afterwards, so I retried using the same duplicate-protection key, which ensures the request runs at most once. The retry worked: **INC-0001** (SEV2, payments-api) is open and has paged on-call. The summary covers the bad deploy, the rollback and the next steps: confirming recovery and finding what's wrong in v5.1.0.\n\nIf you meant a different payments service, tell me which one. Otherwise, v5.1.0 shouldn't be redeployed until the cause is found and fixed.", "type": "text"}]}]}